WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:02.940
- [Narrator] A small city has become one

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:06.090
of the biggest battles in
Russia's war in Ukraine.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:08.490
Moscow has sent tens
of thousands of troops

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:11.400
to Avdiivka in the Eastern Donetsk region.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.610
But Ukraine says, many of
those men have been killed

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:17.580
on the battlefield, in
what's looking like a repeat

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:21.224
of the deadly fight for
Bakhmut earlier this year.

00:00:21.224 --> 00:00:22.057
(tank fires)

00:00:22.057 --> 00:00:24.014
- There's not really
anything left about Avdiivka

00:00:24.014 --> 00:00:25.770
and that's the same as Bakhmut was.

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:27.240
- [Narrator] Here's why
Russia is determined

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.883
to take Avdiivka, no matter the cost.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.660
Capturing Avdiivka would allow Russia

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:36.222
to tighten its grip on the Donetsk region.

00:00:36.222 --> 00:00:37.320
(bomb explodes)

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:41.550
The city is located just over
30 miles south of Bakhmut,

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:44.550
but Avdiivka is more significant to Moscow

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:47.070
because it is close to Donetsk city,

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:50.760
which has been held by Russia since 2014.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:53.010
As with Bakhmut, controlling Avdiivka

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:56.280
won't give Russia any
significant military gains,

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.010
but it would be a
propaganda win for Moscow,

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:02.460
something Ukrainian President
Volodymyr Zelensky says,

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:05.100
his Russian counterpart,
Vladimir Putin needs,

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:06.524
heading into winter.

00:01:06.524 --> 00:01:11.024
- (Volodymyr speaks foreign language)

00:01:15.695 --> 00:01:17.340
- [Narrator] Seizing
Avdiivka would allow Putin

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:21.210
to claim that the momentum in
the war is back with Moscow.

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:25.110
- Putin, after the initial
failure to take Kyiv,

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:30.000
announced that taking the
Donetsk and Luhansk regions

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.100
was the priorities and symbolically,

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.140
it would show that they're
still moving forward.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:36.180
- [Narrator] Russia is pouring
large numbers of troops

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:37.950
into its assault and Avdiivka,

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:40.950
just like in Bakhmut earlier this year.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:43.500
And also as in Bakhmut, Ukraine says,

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.840
this has cost Moscow thousands of men

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:49.590
and dozens of armored vehicles,
yet they've hardly advanced.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:52.110
- For the Russians, a war of attrition

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:54.150
favors them a high casualty war.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:55.350
Attrition favors that,

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:58.200
and they've been more
willing to just throw bodies

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.960
at an area to try to
take it than Ukraine has.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.300
- The Russian Ministry
of Defense didn't respond

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:07.050
to a request for comment
about its assault on Avdiivka.

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:09.660
But Russian President
Vladimir Putin has said,

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:12.060
his forces were conducting active defense

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:13.473
along the whole frontline.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.280
For Ukraine, as with Bakhmut,

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.352
Avdiivka is a symbol of resistance.

00:02:20.352 --> 00:02:24.469
- (Maksim speaks foreign language)

00:02:24.469 --> 00:02:25.302
(gun shots)

00:02:25.302 --> 00:02:27.960
- [Narrator] The city has been
a Russian target since 2014

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.210
where Moscow first
launched a covert invasion

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:32.820
of Ukraine's Donetsk and Luhansk regions.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:33.653
(gun shots)

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:35.460
While Russian forces are largely

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.440
in control of the Donetsk region,

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:40.500
Avdiivka remains a Ukrainian stronghold,

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:43.530
but Kyiv has not placed as
much rhetorical importance

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.990
on the city as it did with Bakhmut.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:49.080
- You had Zelensky in
his nightly addresses

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.540
talking about Bakhmut,
basically every night

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:53.977
for months and months and
months, and he's not doing that

00:02:53.977 --> 00:02:55.080
with Avdiivka in the same way.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:59.700
He has not made it a
symbolic political point

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:01.189
to hold onto it.

00:03:01.189 --> 00:03:02.420
(bomb explodes)

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:03.990
- [Narrator] Kyiv was
criticized for its decision

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:06.870
to defend Bakhmut, rather than retreat,

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:10.884
with critics saying Ukraine
had taken too many casualties.

00:03:10.884 --> 00:03:11.850
(gunshots)

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:15.450
- I wouldn't be surprised if Ukrainians

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:18.630
are more willing to give up Avdiivka,

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:20.460
and I don't know that
they're gonna be so willing

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:23.057
to throw so many men at it
as they were with Bakhmut.

00:03:23.057 --> 00:03:25.890
(gunshots)

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:28.080
- [Narrator] Analysts
say Russia's heavy losses

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:32.130
may undermine Moscow's long-term
offensive capabilities.

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:35.580
As winter approaches, season
control of new territory,

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:37.560
no matter how small, would be seen

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.847
as a win in Moscow's eyes.

00:03:39.847 --> 00:03:40.680
(gunshots)

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.060
That says both sides have struggled

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:44.010
to seize any new territory this year

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:45.870
after troops spent months building up

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:48.180
defensive lines last winter.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:50.400
- It's been very difficult
this year for either side

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:51.780
to significantly move the line,

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:55.260
and it looks like that trend
is continuing in Avdiivka,

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.000
and we'll see if that changes,

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.064
but it doesn't look like it so far.

00:03:59.064 --> 00:04:01.731
(intense music)

